tests/golden/check/ffi-counted-by-states-its-extent.hero:22:42: error[counted_by_shape]: `counted_by` on `p` of `fill_zero` names no extent — `0` states no element at all — a stated extent is the number of elements C reaches, at least one
tests/golden/check/ffi-counted-by-states-its-extent.hero:23:42: error[counted_by_shape]: `counted_by` on `p` of `fill_huge` names no extent — `99999999999999999999` is more elements than an `i64` counts, and no buffer C can be handed holds that many
tests/golden/check/ffi-counted-by-states-its-extent.hero:24:45: error[counted_by_shape]: `counted_by` on `p` of `fill_nowhere` names no extent — `NOPE` names no other parameter of `fill_nowhere` and no `constant` of its group — the extent is the sibling C reads the count from, a constant the group declares from the header, or the number itself
tests/golden/check/ffi-counted-by-states-its-extent.hero:25:43: error[counted_by_shape]: `counted_by` on `p` of `fill_other` names no extent — `OTHER_LEN` is a `constant` of the group of "ffi-counted-by-states-its-extent-other.h", and the extent's macro must be one the header declaring `fill_other` defines — declare the constant in that function's own group
tests/golden/check/ffi-counted-by-states-its-extent.hero:26:43: error[counted_by_shape]: `counted_by` on `p` of `fill_float` names no extent — `FILL_SCALE` is not an integer constant, so it counts no elements — an extent is a whole number of what C's pointer points at
tests/golden/check/ffi-counted-by-states-its-extent.hero:27:31: error[ffi_type]: `[u8]` cannot cross the FFI boundary, and it is an `extern`'s parameter — a C header can declare a number, `bool`, `str`, `ptr`, `cstr`, a function type as a parameter, and a `record` declared in this same group (§4.19)
